{
  "description": "Caller policy examples, applied AFTER verification to the authenticated snapshot with a checkpoint obtained independently of the proof and the server response. The verifier has no freshness setting and no stale verdict. decision is accept when the snapshot's networkId equals the checkpoint's, its rootRound \u003e= requiredRootRound and, if given, its sealTimestampSeconds \u003e= minSealTimestampSeconds (all uint64 comparisons exact). The seal timestamp is a consensus-certified time, not proof of real-time freshness.",
